  "goodToKnow": "Die Einbürgerung is naturalisation, becoming a German citizen. Since the June 2024 reform, applicants usually need five years of legal residence instead of eight, and they may keep their previous citizenship. Requirements include German at B1, the Einbürgerungstest (33 questions on law, society and history) and a commitment to the free democratic order. Record numbers were naturalised in 2024. Plural: die Einbürgerungen."
